1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:02,407
when to actually use a database index, use

2
00:00:02,407 --> 00:00:03,147
it when

3
00:00:03,563 --> 00:00:06,299
a column keeps showing up in your WHERE

4
00:00:06,299 --> 00:00:08,373
clauses, your joins or your ORDER BY

5
00:00:08,373 --> 00:00:10,833
so say you are sorting a million orders by

6
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,727
date, and you only show the first 10

7
00:00:12,727 --> 00:00:15,137
if there's no index, the database has to

8
00:00:15,137 --> 00:00:18,237
look at a million rows and sort them before

9
00:00:18,237 --> 00:00:20,437
it can give you those 10

10
00:00:20,797 --> 00:00:22,668
but with an index, it reads them in order

11
00:00:22,668 --> 00:00:24,350
and stops after the first 10

12
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:27,070
also, when you use EXPLAIN, and you realize

13
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,703
that a query doing a full table scan, and it

14
00:00:29,703 --> 00:00:32,977
is slow, then maybe you need an index there

15
00:00:32,977 --> 00:00:36,347
also, when a table gets more read, like you

16
00:00:36,347 --> 00:00:38,937
read it a lot more than you write it, that's

17
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:40,667
also a good situation for a database index

18
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:42,457
but you shouldn't do that when the table is

19
00:00:42,457 --> 00:00:44,362
small or when table is constantly written to

20
00:00:44,362 --> 00:00:46,817
and rarely searched, then you probably don't

21
00:00:46,817 --> 00:00:48,167
need a database index in that situation
